  "category": "wrong-semantic-output",
  "confidence": "high",
  "rationale": "The agent successfully upgraded the dependencies and adapted the code to pass the test suite in its own environment, but the verifier re-runs the tests with a specific command that installs exact dependency versions (ajv@7.0.2, ajv-keywords@4.0.0, ajv-errors@2.0.0) and then executes the test suite. The verifier output shows 4 tests failing because the agent's error-message transformations (e.g., for minLength/maxLength) are inverted relative to what the installed ajv version actually produces, causing assertion mismatches. The candidate patch therefore produces incorrect semantic output (wrong error messages) under the verifier's exact dependency resolution.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "section": "verifier",
      "quote": "Expected substring: \"'i18n.locales[1]' should NOT have more than 10 characters\"\nReceived message:   \"'i18n.locales[1]' should NOT be longer than 10 characters\""
    },
    {
      "section": "verifier",
      "quote": "Expected substring: \"'i18n.locales[1]' should NOT be shorter than 2 characters\"\nReceived message:   \"'i18n.locales[1]' should NOT have fewer than 2 characters\""
    },
    {
      "section": "candidate_patch",
      "quote": "case 'minLength': {\n            if (newError.message && newError.message.includes('should NOT have fewer than')) {\n              newError = {\n                ...newError,\n                message: newError.message.replace(\n                  'should NOT have fewer than',\n                  'should NOT be shorter than',\n                ),\n              };\n            }"
    }
  ],
